=== tk ===
tk 1.0.0
Minimal task tracker. One JSON document per task in .tasks/ — no daemon, no
index, no database.

Usage: tk [FLAGS] <SUBCOMMAND>

Commands:
  accept   Add or change what must be true for a task to be done
  add      Create a task [aliases: new]
  apply    Apply a batch of intents from stdin under one lock
  block    Add a blocker dependency
  check    Check store integrity (non-zero exit on findings) [aliases: ck]
  config   Show or change configuration
  done     Mark a task done
  drop     Drop a task without doing it
  edit     Edit a task's fields in one write
  init     Create .tasks/ here
  label    Change a task's labels [aliases: tag]
  list     List tasks [aliases: ls]
  lock     Run a command while holding the store mutation lock
  note     Add a log entry [aliases: log]
  path     Print the resolved task store location
  purge    Delete a task [aliases: rm]
  ready    List what can be started now [aliases: rdy]
  show     Show one task
  state    Move a task to a state: open, done, or dropped
  status   Replace the current status (the summary, not the log)
  unblock  Remove a blocker dependency
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Flags:
  -j, --json             Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>        Run in a different directory (or a configured alias)
      --tasks-dir <DIR>  Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                         (no discovery)
  -h, --help             Print help
  -V, --version          Print version

=== tk init ===
Create .tasks/ here

Usage: tk init [--force]

Flags:
      --force            Initialize even if a store already exists here
  -h, --help             Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json             Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>        Run in a different directory (or a configured alias)
      --tasks-dir <DIR>  Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                         (no discovery)

=== tk add ===
Create a task

Usage: tk add [FLAGS] <TITLE>

Arguments:
  <TITLE>  What needs doing

Flags:
  -l, --label <LABEL>     Labels, comma-separated
      --accept <ACCEPT>   What must be true for this to count as done
  -b, --blocked-by <REF>  A ref this task waits on
      --status <STATUS>   A short note about where things stand
  -q, --quiet             Print only the new ref
  -h, --help              Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json              Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>         Run in a different directory (or a configured alias)
      --tasks-dir <DIR>   Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                          (no discovery)

=== tk list ===
List tasks

Usage: tk list [FLAGS]

Flags:
  -q, --search <SEARCH>  Search titles, labels, and status
  -a, --all              Include done and dropped entries
  -s, --state <STATE>    Only this state: open, done, or dropped
  -l, --label <LABEL>    Only this label
      --blocked          Only blocked entries; --no-blocked for unblocked only
      --unblocked        Only unblocked entries
  -n, --limit <LIMIT>    Show at most this many
  -h, --help             Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json             Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>        Run in a different directory (or a configured alias)
      --tasks-dir <DIR>  Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                         (no discovery)

=== tk ready ===
List what can be started now

Usage: tk ready [FLAGS]

Flags:
      --all              Also show what is blocked, marked
  -q, --search <SEARCH>  Search titles, labels, and status
  -l, --label <LABEL>    Only this label
  -n, --limit <LIMIT>    Show at most this many
  -h, --help             Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json             Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>        Run in a different directory (or a configured alias)
      --tasks-dir <DIR>  Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                         (no discovery)

