=== tk edit ===
Edit a task's fields in one write

Usage: tk edit [FLAGS] <REF>

Arguments:
  <REF>  Ref, or part of a title

Flags:
  -t, --title <TITLE>             New title
      --slug <SLUG>               Move the file to a new slug (the ref never
                                  changes)
      --status <STATUS>           Replace the status
      --clear-status              Remove the status
  -l, --label <LABEL>             Replace the whole label set
      --add-label <ADD_LABEL>     Add labels
      --remove-label <REMOVE_LABEL>  Remove labels
      --accept <ACCEPT>           Replace the acceptance criteria
      --add-accept <ADD_ACCEPT>   Add acceptance criteria
      --remove-accept <TEXT>      Remove acceptance criteria
      --clear-accept              Remove every acceptance criterion
  -b, --blocked-by <REF>          Replace the blockers
      --add-block <REF>           Add one blocker
      --remove-block <REF>        Remove one blocker
  -n, --note <NOTE>               Add a log entry along with the rest
      --if-rev <REV>              Refuse if the entry changed since this
                                  revision was read
  -h, --help                      Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json                      Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>                 Run in a different directory (or a configured
                                  alias)
      --tasks-dir <DIR>           Task store directory: exact path, must already
                                  exist (no discovery)

=== tk accept ===
Add or change what must be true for a task to be done

Usage: tk accept [FLAGS] <REF> [CRITERIA]…

Arguments:
  <REF>        Ref, or part of a title
  [CRITERIA]…  Criteria to add

Flags:
      --set <SET>        Replace the whole list
      --remove <TEXT>    Remove a criterion
      --clear            Remove every criterion
      --if-rev <REV>     Refuse if the entry changed since this revision was
                         read
  -h, --help             Print help

Global flags:
  -j, --json             Output as JSON
  -C, --dir <DIR>        Run in a different directory (or a configured alias)
      --tasks-dir <DIR>  Task store directory: exact path, must already exist
                         (no discovery)

